            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="KEA04" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>George</forename>
                        <surname>Kearsley</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1000">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1000"/>
                    <occupation>bookseller</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Kearsley was a bookseller who published <title>Cursory Strictures</title>; his father, also George,
      published <title>Life of Chatham</title>.</p>
                        <p>There are other Kearsleys in the diary but these have been coded as <persName key="KEA01">Thomas Kearsley</persName>, the artist.</p>
                        <p>Note that St Clair refers to James Kearsley, not George. Neither the <title>British Book Trade Index</title> nor the <title>DNB</title> 
    make any metion of a James Kearsley.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title>DNB</title>
                    </bibl>
                    <bibl type="other">
                        <title>British Book Trades Index</title>
                    </bibl>
                    <bibl type="printedbook">St Clair</bibl>
